From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:40:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add the PauseAI CRM: volunteer, chapter and stakeholder
 management

A new SvelteKit + Drizzle + PostgreSQL service in crm/, managed by PauseAI
Global and usable by every national chapter, that integrates with the
systems PauseAI already runs (Airtable, Discord via PauseBot, MailerSend).

What is in this foundation:
- Data model: one `people` table for volunteers, politicians, journalists
  and donors with role profiles; a chapter tree (Global > national > local)
  with materialized paths; identities for external systems; append-only
  consents; one interaction timeline; teams; access grants; project
  templates, tasks, events; a Postgres-backed job queue.
- Airtable import of Members and National groups: incremental cursor,
  idempotent upserts, chapter routing by country, drift report for
  vocabulary values the code does not know.
- Discord: signed PauseBot webhook (HMAC over timestamp and body), identity
  linking including join-form username claims, country roles to chapters,
  outbound role assignment through PauseBot.
- Auth: passwordless magic links, hashed tokens and sessions, bootstrap
  admins. Authz: chapter-subtree and team scoping enforced in SQL, field
  masking by tier.
- Tasks: three built-in "event in a box" templates, relative deadlines,
  reminders before and escalation up the chain after a missed deadline.
- UI: sign-in, my tasks, people, person timeline, chapters, admin (sync
  state, jobs, webhook events, sandbox outbox).
- Docs: architecture, data model, integrations, permissions and security,
  two ADRs (why Postgres rather than Airtable or AtomicServer; relationship
  to the existing PauseAI Everything CRM), roadmap.

Tests run against a real PostgreSQL 16 (24 tests), svelte-check is clean
and the production build succeeds. Email is sandboxed unless
EMAIL_MODE=live.

